    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="ef72278b-814f-5d1a-9d3a-b3d3a03cce11" activityNameId="80ccc801-12ce-5b7f-be34-a18ba3454491" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Silicon, production mix, photovoltaics, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Silicon, production mix, photovoltaics, at plant
Solar-grade silicon (about 99.9999999% = 9N purity) is mainly produced by the modified Siemens process. The share of solar-grade silicon produced in fluidised bed reactors (FBR) is &lt;5% according to ITRPV 2020. This production route is not modelled separately because life cycle inventory data are not available. The share of electronic-grade and electronic off-grade silicon used in the PV industry is considered negligible. Imports of polysilicon are not taken into account since domestic production of polysilicon is sufficient to cover wafer production.;
CAS number: 7440-21-3; 
Formula: Si; 
UUID: ae1fbf93-560b-4eb2-878a-569f82bb5a09
Domestic production and imports of the purified silicon feedstock used for single-crystalline and multi-crystalline silicon wafer production in Asia and Pacific. Transport of polysilicon from different world regions to regional storage.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Modified Siemens process
Time period: Data refer to 2018
Production volume: Approximately 450000 t in 2018
Sampling: Survey among market intelligence companies 
Extrapolations: None
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_ae1fbf93-560b-4eb2-878a-569f82bb5a09.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
